{"status":"completed","summary":"Built and verified the replicated CORP.EXAMPLE Samba AD environment. Both controller-outage scenarios passed, and all services are restored and healthy.","actions_performed":["Provisioned node1 and joined node2 as replicated AD controllers.","Joined node3 as the member file server and node4 as the client.","Bound directory, DNS, Kerberos, and SMB services to the 10.100.79.0/24 identity network.","Created engineering and infrasetuser, then published the writable engineering share with the required welcome file.","Stored the generated user credentials in /root/corp-user.env on node4 as root:root mode 0600.","Tested each controller outage independently, including fresh Kerberos authentication, DNS, machine trust, and SMB write/read/delete operations.","Restored both controllers and removed temporary duplicate credential files while preserving the required node4 environment file."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Replicated CORP.EXAMPLE controllers","command_ids":["cmd-3ceca92d87e04096","cmd-d7bbb4be294c4b3a","cmd-8d8d45a1b3214045","cmd-d9978d9b2c0b4ebc"],"summary":"Node1 provisioned CORP.EXAMPLE, node2 joined as a DC, and both final controller checks report active AD roles, both DC DNS records, healthy DRS, replicated member/client computer objects, and identity-only core listeners."},{"requirement":"Engineering group and infrasetuser membership","command_ids":["cmd-9d2955fe726d4119","cmd-1c956cc6c09f4332"],"summary":"The enabled user was added to engineering on node1; node2 received the objects through replication and issued the user a TGT and LDAP ticket."},{"requirement":"Joined member server, engineering share, permissions, and welcome.txt","command_ids":["cmd-cab187aa41a647b9","cmd-1571f787d12d4ff5","cmd-94d3aa40c7284af2"],"summary":"Node3 reports a healthy join and trust, active smbd/winbind, root:engineering mode 2770 share ownership, exact infraset-samba content, group-restricted write configuration, and SMB bound only to 10.100.79.12. Node4 successfully read and wrote through the share."},{"requirement":"Joined client and protected credential file","command_ids":["cmd-9f26263a1a154fdd","cmd-94d3aa40c7284af2","cmd-62464971909c4de3"],"summary":"Node4 reports Join is OK and healthy trust. The required SAMBA_USER and nonempty SAMBA_PASSWORD keys remain in /root/corp-user.env as root:root mode 0600; auxiliary credential copies were removed."},{"requirement":"Dedicated identity network usage","command_ids":["cmd-8d8d45a1b3214045","cmd-d9978d9b2c0b4ebc","cmd-1571f787d12d4ff5","cmd-94d3aa40c7284af2"],"summary":"Controllers and file server use enp8s0 on 10.100.79.10–12 with no core service binding on management addresses. Node4 routes share traffic over enp8s0 from 10.100.79.13 and uses both identity-network DNS servers."},{"requirement":"Authentication, DNS, and share access with node1 down","command_ids":["cmd-4a4d4f47902740bb","cmd-f48e5b85216c4e71","cmd-761755c98a6f4200","cmd-0d267398aca64313","cmd-613393606dbe418c","cmd-dec70a39f7a84c40","cmd-085fc356de5f446e"],"summary":"After a healthy baseline, node1 was stopped and its identity listeners disappeared. Node2 remained active; node3/node4 selected it, node4 obtained a fresh TGT directly from 10.100.79.11 and completed a new SMB write/read/delete. Node1 was restored and both DRS views recovered."},{"requirement":"Authentication, DNS, and share access with node2 down","command_ids":["cmd-a42fff6e9d2643e3","cmd-4e62b7774b904f61","cmd-06b37cab7f2e43f9","cmd-7da7ce4961cb4210","cmd-becf4ca650784e28","cmd-5ee187406d3244b9","cmd-005e2ea77d4c49f1","cmd-9053a844bfe74c9d"],"summary":"Node2 was stopped after a healthy baseline and its identity listeners disappeared. Node1 remained active; node3/node4 selected it, node4 obtained a fresh TGT directly from 10.100.79.10 and completed a new SMB write/read/delete. Node2 was restarted, became fully ready with zero database errors, and both DRS views returned to healthy."}]}
